From c3961a1bf1f84d6f2103ecaa7b2a856f77565592 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:54:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Done checks: key declared boards and replicas by
 content, one read pass per count

Two things the hermes-mods half of t_28eb8d66d577eab3 needs from core
before kanban-honest-done can stop running on every holder wake.

1. kanban_annotation_parts._done_key keyed every declared file by its
   change signature (stat, header counter, WAL-index header).
   kanban-honest-done reads the boards and their sync replicas, and those
   files are rewritten several times a second by bookkeeping (claims,
   heartbeats, pull stamps): declaring them would have rerun every done
   check on each of those writes, the same rate as declaring nothing. A
   declared board is now left to the attention key's own content
   revisions, and a declared sync replica is keyed by its content
   revision (SHADOW_TABLES). A replica whose revision cannot vouch (stat
   fallback not yet settled, unreadable) makes the key unequal to
   everything, so the checks run. Any other declared file keeps the
   change signature.

2. attention_task_counts enters each check's optional attention_pass (a
   context manager factory carried on the check function) around all the
   cards of one count and closes it with the count. kanban-honest-done
   uses it to share one connection per database across the count instead
   of opening several per card (19% of the annotation thread's samples
   were its ro_connect). A pass that cannot be entered is skipped; the
   check then reads on its own. Nothing is held between counts.

Tests (test_kanban_annotation_parts):
test_a_declared_board_or_replica_reruns_the_checks_on_content_not_on_
bookkeeping and test_a_check_that_offers_a_read_pass_gets_one_around_
all_its_cards_and_it_is_closed. Mutants: keying replicas by stat again
fails the first; keeping declared boards in the stat key fails the
first; not entering the pass fails the second. 182 test files importing
the touched modules: 3308 passed, 0 failed, 1 skipped. scripts/check
--base origin/main: 21 checks ok.

Hermes-Card: t_28eb8d66d577eab3
